{# purpose: declarative data chart (bar/line/pie/scatter/candlestick…) via Apache ECharts, view-time SVG #}
{# `chart` is the shared marker every engine wears; `apache-echarts` selects the engine #}
{# SHIPPED HIDDEN. The spec used to be visible until the engine replaced it,
   which meant every reader watched a block of JSON for as long as the ~900 KB
   engine took to arrive — the spec is data for the engine, not something a
   reader was ever meant to read first. Hidden is the resting state; charts.js
   puts the chart on screen when it has one, or a message where it failed, and
   the source stays in the DOM behind a `show source` button either way.
   The attribute (not a class) so the UA stylesheet hides it even if the
   stylesheet never loads. #}
{% macro apache_echarts(option="", height=340) %}
  <pre class="chart apache-echarts" hidden{% if height != 340 %} data-height="{{ height }}"{% endif %}>
{{ caller() if caller is defined else option }}
  </pre>
{% endmacro %}
